WEBVTT

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.360
Kunimatsu Miki

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:07.860
Ren...

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.360
What?

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.610
If you don't go to bed soon, 
our brother will yell at you.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.080
I know.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.880
If you want me to, I'll be just your brother.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.770
<i>Does that mean something will change?</i>

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:33.010
<i>How is "just my brother" different 
from how things have been?</i>

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.810
Ren, if you can't sleep, 
want me to make you some coffee?

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:18.510
Are you stupid, Shima? 
Why would you give him caffeine?

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:22.790
I know. If you're too hungry to sleep, 
want to get ramen by the station?

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.580
Now?

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.280
I'd rather have udon.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.010
Well, I'm definitely getting 
ramen, and tonkotsu flavor.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:31.330
Right, Ren?

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.060
I want soba.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.880
You must be joking. Soba is for old men.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.600
Aki, you're being prejudiced.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.590
Nah, midnight ramen's gotta be ton—

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:43.150
Stop shouting in the middle of the night.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.100
Ren, you should go to bed already.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:48.060
I'm going to bed.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.460
You're no fun.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:54.100
Go on, head to my room and sleep.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.360
Okay.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:00.070
<i>How are things different from before?</i>

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.230
Bro...

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.250
What?

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.340
"What?" Seriously?

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.080
Why are you making that kid
be so considerate toward you?

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.330
Considerate? Toward me?

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.980
It really is impressive 
how imperceptive you are.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.090
He already ran away once. 
This idiot never learns.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.340
What's with you two?

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:25.320
Normally, he goes straight to 
your room without being told,

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.100
but today he got your permission.

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.940
And he couldn't find an 
opportunity to ask you himself,

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.610
so he was forced to wait until this late.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:38.110
I don't know if I'd call it admirable, 
but it's so awkward, I could cry.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.320
Why are you guys suddenly siding with Ren?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.460
We are his big brothers, after all.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:47.870
Liar. You've acted totally 
disinterested until now.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:53.400
You were just sticking so close to him 
that there was no room for us.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.340
Huh?

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.090
And you're making it sound like it's our fault.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.310
Bro, you're too imperceptive.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.380
If that's not your intention, 
why don't you just tell him so?

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:04.010
What intention?

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.220
To do what you've done with women until now.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.680
I'm sorry!

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.270
Why is he repenting?

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.900
Ren, you're still awake?

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.780
I was just reading since I thought 
it would make me sleepy.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.950
Really? You seemed pretty into—

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.040
Wait, what?

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.040
White Fang?

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.580
That brings back memories.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:37.550
Do you remember how 
I used to read that to you?

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:41.800
I do. I brought this from 
your bookshelf in Canada.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.800
Take good care of it. It's my favorite book.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.070
Yeah.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:48.610
Actually...

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:52.760
You can have this back.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:53.760
Ren?

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.190
If it's important, you should hold on to it.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.650
I guess, but...

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.650
I'm going to sleep.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:06.060
Yeah, yeah. I'll turn off the lights, then.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.200
<i>When I said I would be just his brother,</i>

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.900
<i>Haru didn't respond.</i>

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.300
Huh? Where's Ren?

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.550
He left a while ago.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.490
What? Already?

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.970
I said I'd give him a ride.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.770
You don't have the time, do you?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:33.600
Doesn't construction on the café start today?

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.300
Well...

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.760
I was going to tell him that I won't
be able to give him a ride

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:41.070
for a while after this morning.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:47.440
Hey, that's unusual. Your boyfriend 
didn't come with you today?

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:48.690
Boyfriend?

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:54.320
How was Golden Week? 
Did you go on a date somewhere?

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.410
A date?

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:59.630
I'm asking if you guys had a romantic break!

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.360
Not really.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:05.080
Haru had a female guest who kept stopping by.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:06.380
He's cheating on you?!

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:10.260
And? Was she pretty?

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:14.710
Most of the women who approach 
Haru are confident in themselves.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:15.610
Oh?

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:18.280
If I had to say, she's probably pretty, but...

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:18.990
But?

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.150
I'm not sure.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.470
She seems to have been friends 
with Haru for a long time, but...

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:25.400
But?

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:28.900
I did learn that she doesn't 
think very highly of me.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.620
Of course not.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.930
She probably thinks a woman 
like herself is better than a dude.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:37.470
She said she once confessed her feelings 
to Haru, but he rejected her.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:40.370
Then you're rivals.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.130
We're not rivals.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:47.170
What's this? You're awfully confident.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.030
You think she can't beat you?

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.290
I didn't mean that.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:56.180
<i>I must've been mistaken.</i>

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:59.630
<i>About everything, from the start.</i>

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:12.410
Uh-oh... I'd better go shopping for dinner.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.030
<i>Ren...</i>

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:21.800
I'm bored.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:26.340
Fine, then. I'll read you 
a book, so try to endure it.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.340
I don't need that.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:31.340
Are you sure? This seems like one you'd enjoy.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:39.250
So the gray wolf, White Fang, is one-quarter dog?

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.350
What does that mean?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:46.180
He's like me. White Fang's grandma is a dog,

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:48.420
and his grandpa is a wolf.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:51.110
Does that mean Haruko's father is a wolf?

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:57.030
Hey, Haru, are you listening?

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.250
What, you're here, Kiyoka?

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:03.460
Look at you, spacing out 
in the middle of the day.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:06.920
I came to check on you since 
construction started today.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:09.840
Do you not serve tea to guests here?

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:12.130
What a pain in the butt.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.950
What did you say?

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:15.790
I'll have some iced lemon tea.

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:16.960
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:22.350
What's this ratty old book?

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.990
Ugh, it's in English!

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:26.020
Who the hell would read this?

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:28.600
Both Ren and I grew up speaking English.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:32.490
Is that kid so quiet because 
he's not good at Japanese?

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.210
Quiet? You mean Ren?

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:37.530
He's way better now than when I met him.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:42.610
He wouldn't say a word, but he'd 
glare at me, bite me, and scratch me.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.560
He used to try to threaten me all the time.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:49.000
What stray dog are you talking about?

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:52.570
Your youngest brother is adopted?

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:55.450
No wonder he sticks so closely to you.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.460
So what?

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.930
What does it matter that Ren is adopted?

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:03.640
It doesn't, really.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.440
I read this book when I was a kid.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.950
A lonely wolf

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:13.890
meets the only man he ever 
acknowledges as his master, right?

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:17.200
Because he showed him kindness 
for the first time in his life.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:20.950
But that's just imprinting.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:23.950
Just like that kid.

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:29.710
Damn that woman! She's right on the money.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.900
I know that better than anyone else.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:34.120
Haru?

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:36.660
Are you going out?

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.000
Oh, yeah... Welcome home.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.510
I was about to go buy stuff for dinner.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.800
Anyway, sorry I couldn't 
drive you to and from school.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:47.490
I can do it myself.

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:51.480
You're going to be busy from now on, 
right? Do you need any help?

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.440
You're such a good kid, Ren.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.330
Take Tanuki for his walk, then.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:01.490
There's pudding in the refrigerator. 
You can have it later.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:03.490
You always do that!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:04.830
Ren?

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.250
Never mind. It's nothing.

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.790
I'll take him for a walk, 
and I'll eat the pudding, too.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:10.750
Hey, Ren...

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.250
If you keep talking to me, I'll hit you.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.040
H-Hit me?

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:18.200
<i>Being happy about getting praised like a child</i>

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:21.330
<i>and getting angry about 
being treated like a child</i>

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:24.530
<i>make me want to shout at him.</i>

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:30.080
<i>It's like nothing has changed 
since I was eight years old.</i>

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:32.870
<i>Neither me nor Haru.</i>

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:44.950
Ren?

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:49.660
I have an assignment. I'm not done yet.

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:51.460
I'll sleep in here tonight.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:52.960
Got it.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:54.480
Sounds rough.

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:00.470
What are you doing?

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.260
What am I doing?

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:05.750
A single is a tight fit for two, 
but just one night won't be too bad.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.220
I'm going to sleep first.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.730
<i>This guy...</i>

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:15.570
You're going to sleep next to me while
I struggle with Modern Japanese? Huh?!

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:17.990
Ow, ow! You're pulling my hair!

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.310
It's not like I can help you.

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:21.990
Go back to your room!

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:26.120
I don't want to. I can't sleep without you.

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:28.690
Don't lie!

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.120
I'm not lying.

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:32.250
Hey, Ren...

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:34.360
Are you avoiding me?

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:40.830
I'm not avoiding you. 
I'm talking to you right now.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.110
Then are you afraid of me?

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:45.430
Why would I be afraid of you?

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:49.980
Because, the other day, I did 
something awful to you here.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:51.980
You were just drunk.

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:55.650
You said you wouldn't lay a finger on me.

00:11:56.810 --> 00:11:57.980
Haru...

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.490
You're important to me.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.340
When I think about what 
I'd do if you hated me...

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:08.300
When I think you might leave me 
and go back to Canada again,

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.790
I can't do anything all day.

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:17.710
<i>Haru wants a kind family 
who will always be by his side,</i>

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:21.240
<i>and younger brothers who need him,
whom he can protect.</i>

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:26.290
<i>When he realizes I'm neither of those things...</i>

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:28.010
I won't go back.

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.000
I wanted to be with you.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.500
So I won't go back.

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:37.530
I'll stay here with you.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.060
<i>He'll...</i>

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:43.250
<i>Haru will probably be disappointed with me.</i>

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:50.410
Damn... I let him fall asleep 
before his assignment was done.

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:54.420
I know what Aki and Shima said,

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:56.920
but normally you wouldn't sleep this deeply

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:59.920
in front of someone you loved.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:08.590
Haru?

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:09.760
Hey, good morning.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:13.880
Did I fall asleep after that last night?

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:15.300
Well, yeah.

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.260
My Modern Japanese assignment!

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:20.690
Good luck.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:24.340
Don't you ever come back into this room!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:26.700
As a scholarship student, Ren's assignments 
are also taken into consideration.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:32.320
What's this? Ren, what are you doing?

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:33.700
My Modern Japanese assignment.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.490
Modern Japanese?

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:38.950
I'm exempt from taking English, 
so I get this instead.

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:40.710
Exempt? Why?

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:44.820
Because my Japanese isn't as good 
since I returned from living abroad.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:49.800
In your case, you know hardly anything 
about what young people are like.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:51.970
Uh, Kaidou?

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:54.690
You have a visitor from the girls' building.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.480
Hey.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.610
Who's that boyish-looking chick?

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:01.350
Kiri...

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:04.610
Ren, how have you been?

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.180
I haven't had a chance to 
get out of the girls' building.

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:08.860
I was finally able to come see you.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:13.030
Come to think of it, everyone in the 
neighborhood's saying you're opening a café.

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:15.330
Your brother's pretty famous.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.450
Really?

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:19.730
So, aren't you going to introduce me to her?

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:21.160
I don't see any need for that.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:22.130
Hey!

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:25.270
This is Kurosaki Juuzen, 
and that's Kondou Kiri.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:28.100
Actually, Kiri, I'm glad you're here.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.290
I'm having trouble with my 
Modern Japanese assignment.

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.430
Could you check it for me?

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:32.280
Sure.

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:35.720
Hey, it's just an essay. What's the theme?

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.480
"Something fun that happened recently."

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:40.010
Okay, let me see...

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:42.290
"I went to a nearby zoo with Haru.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:43.540
I saw raccoon dogs.

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:46.500
I was shocked by how much 
they looked like our pet, Tanuki."

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:49.640
What is this, the diary 
of a kid in grade school?

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:50.990
Don't read it out loud!

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.700
Ren, you have a raccoon dog at home?

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:55.250
It's a dog.

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:58.700
I see you have the emotional 
complexity of a grade-school student.

00:14:58.700 --> 00:14:59.650
15 points.

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:00.750
15...

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:03.460
Everyone has their strengths and weaknesses.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:08.400
This isn't your kind of assignment, 
but it's been assigned to you.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.510
If you don't use your left brain, it'll atrophy.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.940
I think you are right...

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:15.510
What's up with this intellectual conversation?

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:18.220
Well, I'm heading back.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:20.320
What?

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:23.770
Oh, I just thought you looked a bit pale.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:26.030
Did your assignment keep you up last night?

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:29.870
I fell asleep yesterday while 
working on my assignment.

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:30.820
I see.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:34.000
If you didn't get enough sleep, 
go to the nurse's office.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:34.980
Got it.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:40.950
Hey, Ren, are you okay?

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:44.310
Actually, I'm having a harder time
slowing down to match your pace.

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.570
I'm going ahead.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.420
What?! You must be joking, Ren!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:50.340
He's fast. Who is that?

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.680
Isn't that Kaidou, the kid 
who was living abroad?

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:57.300
<i>I haven't even run that far, 
and I'm short of breath.</i>

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:01.350
<i>In Canada, I was always 
running at the dogs' pace.</i>

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:06.320
<i>Come to think of it, lately I've 
only been going out to walk Tanuki.</i>

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.580
Kaidou, you've got the fastest time.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:14.490
You're so fast. Kids raised in 
the Rockies sure are different.

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:19.080
<i>Once Tanuki gets used to being outside...</i>

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:20.550
What's wrong?

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.460
K-Kaidou!

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:28.090
<i>I'll need to take him on more walks.</i>

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:31.720
What? Ren did?

00:16:32.230 --> 00:16:35.220
Yes, I'll come pick him up right away.

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.300
Thank you.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:41.230
Kiyo, sorry, but could you handle the rest?

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.360
I need to go pick up Ren.

00:16:43.840 --> 00:16:45.770
Can't he come home by himself?

00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:49.640
There's no way. He had a fever this morning.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:51.390
And you let him go to school?

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:54.310
He said he had an important 
assignment to turn in today.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:56.120
Oh, right, Kiyo...

00:16:57.640 --> 00:17:01.370
You can have this back. I don't need it.

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:03.450
You didn't call her?

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:06.630
I don't need to call. She probably 
doesn't need it, either.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:10.970
You're right. She's getting married soon.

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:14.610
That's why she wanted to apologize 
for hurting you in the past.

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:18.450
She said she hopes you're 
happily in love with someone now.

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:21.140
See? It's not necessary at all.

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:22.890
<i>After all,</i>

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:27.260
<i>both our minds are probably 
filled with someone else now.</i>

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:29.860
Ren!

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:31.900
Juuzen...

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:36.900
You scared me! You suddenly 
collapsed after you finished running.

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:40.050
And there's no nurse on duty today, of all days.

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:40.990
Kaidou.

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:45.230
I called your brother. 
He's coming to pick you up.

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:48.940
Sorry for causing you trouble.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:50.950
You're drenched in sweat. 
Want to get changed?

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:51.670
Yeah.

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:54.420
What is it, Kurosaki?

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:57.430
Nothing, nothing! Sorry!

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.340
Okay... Thanks for handling this, then.

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.380
Ren, be straight with me!

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:08.060
About what?

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.880
Isn't he cheating on you?

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:11.730
No.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:12.950
Then you're cheating on him?

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:14.070
No.

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:16.890
What's going on between you, then?

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.370
Nothing.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:20.020
Does that mean you're back together?

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:20.820
Back together?

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:22.820
You're making this difficult!

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:25.970
If there's nothing going on, 
you wouldn't come to school with this!

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:27.690
Let me see that again!

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:29.760
Stop, Juuzen! Let go!

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.590
Just let me see it!

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:33.400
Hey.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.840
Kurosaki-kun, right?

00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:39.630
What are you doing to my Ren?

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:45.530
Did he see it?

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:46.350
See what?

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:50.230
You have a fever of 38 degrees.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:51.980
That's cold...

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:53.620
Do you feel sick?

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:56.490
Haru...

00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:57.740
What?

00:18:58.300 --> 00:19:01.100
Didn't you say you wouldn't 
make a move on your brother?

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.440
Try calling me Brother, then.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:08.910
It's "Brother."

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:12.710
If you don't make it sound cute, I won't pass you.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:16.550
<i>If Ren would call me that,</i>

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.050
<i>I'd be just his brother.</i>

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:23.360
<i>But somewhere inside me, I hope he won't.</i>

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.390
Go on, say it.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:27.770
I...

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.490
can't say that, you pervert!

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:35.900
Several 
Days 
Later

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:35.210
This is raw whitebait?

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:37.400
I've never had it before. It's good.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:41.210
I'm glad you're feeling better, though.

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:42.910
I'm fine now.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:46.390
So he's your brother, not your boyfriend, huh?

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:48.940
Haru's not my brother.

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:49.790
What?!

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:53.490
So he did give you that hickey on your neck?

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:55.420
My neck? Hickey?

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:56.860
Yeah, right here.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:19:59.910
Wait, you have a new one now!

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:00.710
Where?

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:03.660
Right here! What's wrong with your brother?

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:06.800
Could there be more? Let me see!

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:07.930
Stop!

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:10.130
Show me!

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:12.780
What are you doing to my Ren?

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:17.260
Y-You're mistaken!

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:19.320
Haru, stop that.

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:22.500
Your youngest brother's friend 
came over bearing gifts,

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.520
so why would you bully him?

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:25.300
Right?

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:26.580
Ba-dump

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:31.380
Um, my name's Kurosaki Juuzen. 
What's your name, miss?

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:33.500
I'm Kiyoka. Nice to meet you.

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:35.080
It's too bad, though.

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:39.840
I'm actually not a miss, but a mister.

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:41.220
Huh?!

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:46.510
Real Name: 
Takamori Seiji

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.750
Did I scare you?

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.510
No wonder she doesn't smell like a woman.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:48.710
You know people by their smells?

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:50.980
Yeah. I know your smell, too.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:52.060
Mine?

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.800
I like it. It's calming.

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:58.590
I really like your smell, too. 
You kind of smell...

00:20:58.590 --> 00:20:59.590
Like a dad.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.880
Brother, customers are starting to show up...

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.320
Ren, is something wrong?

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.360
Nope.

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:09.220
Ah, there you are.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:14.500
This is the café's sign. 
Ren Ren, could you put it up for us?

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:16.960
After all, it's opening day.

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:18.330
Me?

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:25.010
Did you know Haru-san 
opened this café for you?

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:26.760
For me?

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:31.340
He said you'd been getting fevers 
a lot since you moved to Japan,

00:21:31.340 --> 00:21:34.940
so he said he'd make sure you 
got whatever you wanted to eat.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:40.550
So he got a cooking license and opened 
a place to eat next to the house.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:44.260
He was also worried that 
you're not getting taller.

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:48.160
He doesn't need to worry about that.

00:21:48.520 --> 00:21:49.950
Welcome!

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Next Time
